      "description": "We used to have a pretty clear idea of what an autocrat was. History is full of examples: Adolf Hitler, Joseph Stalin, Mao Zedong, along with Vladimir Putin, Xi Jinping and Viktor Orban today. The list goes on.\n\nSo, where does US President Donald Trump fit in?\n\nIn The Conversation's new podcast, The Making of an Autocrat, we asked six experts on authoritarianism and US politics to explain exactly how an autocrat is made — and whether Trump is on his way to becoming one.\n\nThis is the step-by-step guide Trump is following, tried and tested the world over by the strongmen Trump seeks to emulate.",
